         "step": 1,
         "text": "Differentiate both sides of \\( \\sin\\left(g(x)\\right) = \\frac{2 x}{11} \\) with respect to x. The chain rule on the left gives \\( \\cos\\left(g(x)\\right) \\cdot g'(x) = \\frac{2}{11} \\).",
         "rule_named": "chain rule on the identity f(g(x)) = x"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Express the trigonometric factor in x by the Pythagorean identity, with the positive root because the cosine is not negative on this branch: \\( \\cos\\left(g(x)\\right) = \\sqrt{1 - \\sin^{2}\\left(g(x)\\right)} = \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{4 x^{2}}{121}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "Pythagorean identity on the principal branch"
      },
